OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F317A1783673336
OL,3,CFerrari's Charles Leclerc wins British
OL,4,CGrand Prix
OL,6,FIn another late twist, Max Verstappen
OL,7,Fcrashed out at Stowe on the 48th lap
OL,8,Fof 52 while running in third place.
OL,10,FWith Verstappen's Red Bull stranded in
OL,11,Fthe gravel in front of 16,000 Lando
OL,12,FNorris supporters at the world
OL,13,Fchampion's designated stand, the
OL,14,Fsafety car was deployed.
OL,16,FLeader Leclerc and Hamilton both
OL,17,Fstopped for new tyres, but Russell
OL,18,Fremained out on track which elevated
OL,19,Fhim to second place.
OL,1,W~s1{$~k4{$k7                    G2/4
OL,2,W,.!/  +.!/*%*%R,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,RpppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/sport
OL,24,ANext Page BNat Sport CNat Radio FRewind
FL,318,300,200,120,000,100
PN,31703
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F317A1783673336
OL,3,CFerrari's Charles Leclerc wins British
OL,4,CGrand Prix
OL,6,FThe safety car looked set to peel in
OL,7,Fto provide a one-lap grandstand
OL,8,Ffinish, but it remained on track, with
OL,9,FLeclerc taking the win ahead of
OL,10,FRussell and Hamilton. Lando Norris
OL,11,Ffinished fourth.
OL,13,FAntonelli took the chequered flag in
OL,14,Fninth but he was dealt a five-second
OL,15,Fpenalty for exceeding track limits as
OL,16,Fhe ran off the circuit on multiple
OL,17,Foccasions in his "broken" Mercedes to
OL,18,Fleave him pointless in 16th.
